WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:06.973
[ Indistinct whispering ]

00:00:06.973 --> 00:00:10.110
-Remember the Lego thing?
-Yeah.

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:13.113
-I made it right now
and it was the first one.

00:00:13.113 --> 00:00:17.650
[ Whispering indistinctly ]

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:19.352
-Oh, you did?
-Yeah.

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:21.320
-That's so cool. Alright, good.
I'll be right out.

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:24.156 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:24.156 --> 00:00:26.092
Hello, everybody, and welcome
to another edition of

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:31.297
"The Tonight Sbow" starring
Jimmy Fallon, at-home edition.

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:33.133
Thank you very much
for tuning in.

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:38.037
This is week four, everybody,
and it feels like week four.

00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:39.606
But this is it, guys.

00:00:39.606 --> 00:00:41.007
This is -- We're at the top.

00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:42.308
We're at the top of the hill.

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:44.577
We're almost at the top,
so we've got to keep going,

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:47.046
keep pushing each other,
keep supporting each other.

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:49.849
We got this.
We got this, alright?

00:00:49.849 --> 00:00:52.318
Let's get through this week.

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:53.753
Monday's basically already done.

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:55.788
So now we got Tuesday,
Wednesday, Thursday, Friday.

00:00:55.788 --> 00:00:58.391
Four more days.
We're already in. We're in.

00:00:58.391 --> 00:01:01.427
So we're going to have
a big show, a fun show tonight.

00:01:01.427 --> 00:01:03.062
The one and only Lady Gaga

00:01:03.062 --> 00:01:04.830
will be our guest
on the show tonight.

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:09.802
And she is spearheading
the WHO Global Citizen's special

00:01:09.802 --> 00:01:12.504
"One World Together at Home."

00:01:12.504 --> 00:01:14.741
This is her website here.

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:16.676 line:0%
Global citizens.

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:20.680 line:0%
Globalcitizen.org
/togetherathome.

00:01:23.082 --> 00:01:27.420
She's going to talk about
that giant event, April 18th.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:32.291
I am co-hosting it with Jimmy
Kimmel and Stephen Colbert.

00:01:32.291 --> 00:01:34.560
I'm very excited about it.
A lot of big names.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:36.796
And then she has
a little surprise coming up

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:39.098
later in the show
that should be very fun.

00:01:39.098 --> 00:01:42.101
Also my other guest
is Andy Cohen, who we love,

00:01:42.101 --> 00:01:43.837
from "Watch What Happens Live."

00:01:43.837 --> 00:01:46.105
He's doing it from home as well.

00:01:46.105 --> 00:01:48.574
And he's recovering at home.

00:01:48.574 --> 00:01:51.811
He got coronavirus
probably three weeks ago.

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:54.713
And he's going to tell us
about what he went through

00:01:54.713 --> 00:01:56.282
and how he's feeling.

00:01:56.282 --> 00:02:01.154 line:0%
And his charity is
bethennyscause.org.

00:02:01.154 --> 00:02:03.556 line:0%
Bethenny Frankel's charity,

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:06.892 line:0%
which is doing amazing stuff for
disaster relief.

00:02:06.892 --> 00:02:10.029
She is doing some cool,
some cool, cool stuff.

00:02:10.029 --> 00:02:11.631
And then we're going to
finish the show

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:14.334
with Billie Joe Armstrong
from Green Day

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:17.036
doing a cover of
Tommy James and the Shondells'

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:18.404
"I Think We're Alone Now."

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:19.705
It's going to be a great show.

00:02:19.705 --> 00:02:24.310
But first here's the monologue.

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:27.213 line:0%
♪♪

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:29.214
Become to "Tonight Show
At-Home Edition."

00:02:29.214 --> 00:02:31.884
Guys, it is now week four
of being in quarantine.

00:02:31.884 --> 00:02:34.621
That's right. I've spent
four weeks building stuff,

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:36.823
doing chores,
and teaching my own kids.

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:40.326
I feel like I'm one solid beard
away from being Amish.

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:45.798
Well, earlier tonight ABC aired
two hours of "Family Feud."

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:48.000
I got to be honest.
After four weeks in quarantine,

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:52.171
I think we're all
set on family feuds.

00:02:52.171 --> 00:02:54.940
Some business news --
Ben &amp; Jerry's has introduced

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:57.210
a new flavor called
Chip Happens.

00:02:57.210 --> 00:03:00.046
Although I think right now
a more helpful flavor

00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:05.384
would have been
Stay the Fudge Home!

00:03:05.384 --> 00:03:06.952
I betcha Jerry's laughing.

00:03:06.952 --> 00:03:09.922
I don't know about Ben.
He's a harder nut to crack.

00:03:09.922 --> 00:03:11.991
The White House is warning
Americans to avoid

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:15.728
the grocery store or pharmacy
over the next two weeks.

00:03:15.728 --> 00:03:19.332
Right now my idea to keep
two weeks of Xanax smoothies

00:03:19.332 --> 00:03:23.335
in the freezer
is looking pretty good.

00:03:23.335 --> 00:03:25.738
There are still over
a dozen cruise ships circling

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:28.107
around the sea because
they have no place to dock.

00:03:28.107 --> 00:03:31.009
I feel bad for everyone, but
mostly the cruise ship comic

00:03:31.009 --> 00:03:34.914
who's on day 20 of "So anyone
else from out of town?

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:38.918
Not you again, Darrell.
We already talked."

00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:41.020
Michael Jackson's
famous white glove

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:43.856
was auctioned off for $100,000.

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:45.792
The buyer was like,
"Great, I just need one more

00:03:45.792 --> 00:03:49.728
and I can go to
the grocery store."

00:03:49.728 --> 00:03:52.198
A new trend during the pandemic
is a lot of people

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:55.134
are now having their wedding
ceremonies over Zoom.

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:57.203
New couples say they'll
never forget the moment

00:03:57.203 --> 00:04:05.411
when the priest said,
"You may now...the bride."

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:07.579
Meanwhile, a couple in Michigan
got married,

00:04:07.579 --> 00:04:09.282
and they filled the church pews

00:04:09.282 --> 00:04:11.017
with cardboard cutouts
of people.

00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:12.518
It was all fun
until the priest asked

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:13.619
if there were any objections

00:04:13.619 --> 00:04:19.792
and one of the cutouts
raised its hand.

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:23.028
A county in Florida is reminding
residents to remain --

00:04:23.028 --> 00:04:26.265
to maintain a distance of
at least one large alligator

00:04:26.265 --> 00:04:27.599
between each other.

00:04:27.599 --> 00:04:30.503
That's right. A county in
Florida is reminding residents

00:04:30.503 --> 00:04:33.339
to maintain a distance of
at least one large alligator

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:34.774
between each other.

00:04:34.774 --> 00:04:37.410
While in L.A., they're asking
people to keep a distance of

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:41.647
at least three Kevin Harts.

00:04:41.647 --> 00:04:45.117
And finally, today New York City
closed all its dog parks,

00:04:45.117 --> 00:04:46.819
which should explain
why your neighbor

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:49.088
is now holding his dog's butt
out the window.

00:04:49.088 --> 00:04:51.257
There you go, everybody.
That is my monologue.

